WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.722 --> 00:00:07.390
&gt;&gt;&gt; We're back with our politics

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:07.490
lead.

00:00:07.624 --> 00:00:10.493
A trump aligned super pac is

00:00:10.627 --> 00:00:13.396
demanding a Florida ethics

00:00:13.396 --> 00:00:15.632
investigation into whether

00:00:15.765 --> 00:00:17.500
Florida governor Ron Desantis'

00:00:17.634 --> 00:00:19.402
political activities is

00:00:19.469 --> 00:00:20.536
violating state law, accusing

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:22.438
him of running shadow

00:00:22.572 --> 00:00:25.408
presidential campaign, saying

00:00:25.408 --> 00:00:27.410
Ron Desantis should have to

00:00:27.443 --> 00:00:28.044
resign from office.

00:00:28.177 --> 00:00:30.913
Let's discuss.

00:00:31.047 --> 00:00:32.382
Gloria, what do you make of

00:00:32.515 --> 00:00:32.849
this?

00:00:32.982 --> 00:00:35.752
&gt;&gt; Well, an ethics complaint

00:00:35.885 --> 00:00:37.420
filed by friends of Donald Trump

00:00:37.453 --> 00:00:38.788
is something I have a hard time

00:00:38.921 --> 00:00:40.823
getting my arms around, but it's

00:00:40.957 --> 00:00:42.492
a nuisance lawsuit.

00:00:42.625 --> 00:00:44.961
Have you ever met a politician

00:00:45.094 --> 00:00:47.964
who was holding one elected

00:00:48.097 --> 00:00:49.432
office while seeking another?

00:00:49.499 --> 00:00:49.899
I've never met one.

00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:52.502
Every one of them is.

00:00:52.635 --> 00:00:55.071
So this is just -- gives us an

00:00:55.438 --> 00:00:56.239
indication that Donald Trump and

00:00:56.372 --> 00:00:59.008
his friends are willing to throw

00:00:59.442 --> 00:01:01.444
everything they possibly can at

00:01:01.444 --> 00:01:04.747
any time, at any moment against

00:01:04.881 --> 00:01:05.448
Ron Desantis.

00:01:05.448 --> 00:01:07.550
&gt;&gt; There's much more to come.

00:01:07.684 --> 00:01:10.386
We saw a poll yesterday, a CNN

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:11.587
poll, with Republican voters.

00:01:11.721 --> 00:01:14.390
Trump at 40%, Desantis at 36%.

00:01:14.524 --> 00:01:15.792
That's basically a tie.

00:01:15.925 --> 00:01:18.394
&gt;&gt; It shows just how much

00:01:18.528 --> 00:01:19.896
Desantis is on his mind.

00:01:20.029 --> 00:01:21.864
We're already starting to see

00:01:21.998 --> 00:01:22.665
some factions sort of

00:01:22.799 --> 00:01:23.966
development in this early

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:25.535
contest for the Republican

00:01:25.668 --> 00:01:26.869
nomination.

00:01:27.003 --> 00:01:29.472
You can already see pence and

00:01:29.472 --> 00:01:30.840
Nikki Haley on one side, as well

00:01:30.973 --> 00:01:34.410
as Desantis and trump trying to

00:01:34.544 --> 00:01:36.379
compete for a similar base, as

00:01:36.512 --> 00:01:36.679
well.

00:01:36.813 --> 00:01:38.648
You can point to the recent

00:01:38.781 --> 00:01:39.982
comments about Ukraine that

00:01:40.116 --> 00:01:42.051
Desantis made as well, which

00:01:42.185 --> 00:01:43.152
aligns with trump's stance

00:01:43.486 --> 00:01:43.553
before hand.

00:01:43.686 --> 00:01:45.588
So we're seeing these two take

00:01:45.722 --> 00:01:46.456
jabs at each other.

00:01:46.589 --> 00:01:48.324
And what's hanging over it is

00:01:48.458 --> 00:01:50.326
the fact that they seem to be

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:55.732
trying to outtrump one another

00:01:55.865 --> 00:01:56.766
and compete for the base.

00:01:56.899 --> 00:02:00.703
&gt;&gt; There's a new poll out from

00:02:00.837 --> 00:02:03.506
quinnipiac in favor of Desantis,

00:02:03.506 --> 00:02:04.574
it's with independent voters.

00:02:04.707 --> 00:02:07.143
In a head-to-head matchup, 49%

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:09.912
of independents favor Desantis

00:02:10.046 --> 00:02:11.614
over Biden, Biden 45%.

00:02:11.748 --> 00:02:13.883
But then you have a biden/trump

00:02:14.016 --> 00:02:15.985
matchup, and 50% of independents

00:02:16.119 --> 00:02:18.321
go to Biden, versus 42% for

00:02:18.454 --> 00:02:18.921
trump.

00:02:19.055 --> 00:02:21.624
Obviously, it's way early, and

00:02:21.758 --> 00:02:23.926
Desantis hasn't even announced a

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:26.496
candidacy.

00:02:26.629 --> 00:02:29.532
As you know, Republicans lost

00:02:29.532 --> 00:02:33.603
independents by a wide margin in

00:02:33.736 --> 00:02:33.903
2018.

00:02:34.036 --> 00:02:37.540
In 2020, they split evenly with

00:02:37.673 --> 00:02:37.840
them.

00:02:37.974 --> 00:02:39.542
This is a strong argument for

00:02:39.575 --> 00:02:39.876
Ron Desantis.

00:02:40.009 --> 00:02:41.544
&gt;&gt; I don't know if you're going

00:02:41.577 --> 00:02:43.746
to win independents by waging

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:45.715
war on business, waging culture

00:02:45.848 --> 00:02:46.015
wars.

00:02:46.149 --> 00:02:47.750
There's still a lot of tires to

00:02:47.884 --> 00:02:50.219
be kicked when it comes to Ron

00:02:50.353 --> 00:02:50.953
Desantis for voters in Iowa and

00:02:51.087 --> 00:02:55.224
New Hampshire.

00:02:55.558 --> 00:02:57.026
I don't think that the

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.628
independents will be -- I don't

00:02:58.761 --> 00:03:00.296
think independents will go for

00:03:00.429 --> 00:03:01.130
Ron Desantis once he gets

00:03:01.564 --> 00:03:03.199
through a primary.

00:03:03.566 --> 00:03:06.235
I think at this point in 1995,

00:03:06.369 --> 00:03:07.603
Bill Clinton was worried about

00:03:07.737 --> 00:03:08.404
Lamar Alexander.

00:03:08.538 --> 00:03:11.574
&gt;&gt; I think you may be able to

00:03:11.641 --> 00:03:15.945
win independents by going to war

00:03:16.078 --> 00:03:17.747
with Wall Street.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.248
I think that poll number you

00:03:19.582 --> 00:03:21.584
just showed, look, I know

00:03:21.584 --> 00:03:22.485
Republicans don't trust polls.

00:03:22.618 --> 00:03:23.252
I'm a Republican pollster, I

00:03:23.586 --> 00:03:25.154
hear it all the time.

00:03:25.588 --> 00:03:27.590
But numbers like that are the

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:28.357
best thing Ron Desantis has

00:03:28.491 --> 00:03:29.091
going for him.

00:03:29.225 --> 00:03:30.760
Because for years, I said the

00:03:30.893 --> 00:03:31.727
number one thing I hear from

00:03:31.861 --> 00:03:33.629
Republican voters is they want

00:03:33.763 --> 00:03:35.131
someone who fights, they want

00:03:35.264 --> 00:03:36.265
someone who fights.

00:03:36.399 --> 00:03:38.067
After these midterms, they want

00:03:38.201 --> 00:03:38.768
someone who wins.

00:03:38.901 --> 00:03:40.002
The fight is not enough.

00:03:40.136 --> 00:03:41.204
You have to fight and win.

00:03:41.604 --> 00:03:42.805
And if there is a perception out

00:03:42.939 --> 00:03:44.273
there that grows that Donald

00:03:44.407 --> 00:03:46.375
Trump is just not the guy to win

00:03:46.509 --> 00:03:47.677
any more.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:50.279
He's good at throwing punches

00:03:50.413 --> 00:03:52.081
but not good at landing them as

00:03:52.215 --> 00:03:53.616
much, and Ron Desantis is the

00:03:53.616 --> 00:03:55.785
winner, that helps him eat into

00:03:55.918 --> 00:03:56.485
that trump base.

00:03:56.619 --> 00:03:59.622
Not all the way, but that's the

00:03:59.622 --> 00:04:00.022
strongest thing going.

00:04:00.156 --> 00:04:01.624
&gt;&gt; What was interesting in our

00:04:01.624 --> 00:04:03.626
poll yesterday is that it showed

00:04:03.626 --> 00:04:04.927
Republicans really care more

00:04:05.061 --> 00:04:06.195
about a candidate who shares

00:04:06.329 --> 00:04:07.930
their values rather than a

00:04:08.064 --> 00:04:09.232
candidate who can win, which was

00:04:09.632 --> 00:04:11.834
stunning to me.

00:04:11.968 --> 00:04:14.237
But these are trump supporters,

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:14.737
obviously.

00:04:14.871 --> 00:04:15.037
Right?

00:04:15.171 --> 00:04:16.439
And so that's kind of a shift

00:04:16.572 --> 00:04:18.341
that we have seen over the last

00:04:18.474 --> 00:04:19.842
what, four to six years maybe?

00:04:19.976 --> 00:04:22.945
&gt;&gt; What do you make of the fact

00:04:23.079 --> 00:04:24.614
that Desantis has -- his

00:04:24.747 --> 00:04:26.115
position on Ukraine doesn't

00:04:26.249 --> 00:04:27.950
sound the same as his position

00:04:28.084 --> 00:04:28.651
in 2014?

00:04:28.784 --> 00:04:31.654
Obviously, different

00:04:31.654 --> 00:04:32.488
circumstances, et cetera.

00:04:32.622 --> 00:04:37.293
He came out and said skrain not

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:39.662
-- Ukraine is not a vital

00:04:39.662 --> 00:04:40.463
interest to the United States.

00:04:40.596 --> 00:04:42.765
Here are some of the more

00:04:42.899 --> 00:04:43.666
establishment Republicans

00:04:43.666 --> 00:04:46.802
disagreeing with Ron Desantis.

00:04:46.936 --> 00:04:48.371
&gt;&gt; I have a different point of

00:04:48.504 --> 00:04:48.671
view.

00:04:49.739 --> 00:04:51.107
I believe it's very much in the

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:52.775
interest of America to honor our

00:04:52.909 --> 00:04:53.242
word.

00:04:53.676 --> 00:04:55.678
&gt;&gt; I can't imagine what XI

00:04:55.745 --> 00:04:57.046
jinping or the leadership in

00:04:57.179 --> 00:04:58.547
Iran would think if we took that

00:04:58.681 --> 00:04:59.682
course of action.

00:04:59.682 --> 00:05:01.284
&gt;&gt; To say this doesn't matter is

00:05:01.684 --> 00:05:02.919
to say that war crimes don't

00:05:03.052 --> 00:05:03.252
matter.

00:05:03.686 --> 00:05:04.520
&gt;&gt; I don't know what he's trying

00:05:04.654 --> 00:05:05.721
to do or the goal.

00:05:05.855 --> 00:05:07.256
Obviously, he doesn't deal with

00:05:07.690 --> 00:05:09.892
foreign policy every day.

00:05:10.026 --> 00:05:10.793
&gt;&gt; I think this is a much bigger

00:05:10.927 --> 00:05:12.361
issue than a territorial

00:05:12.495 --> 00:05:12.695
dispute.

00:05:12.828 --> 00:05:14.330
&gt;&gt; But my question is, does that

00:05:14.463 --> 00:05:16.432
help Desantis with the base?

00:05:16.565 --> 00:05:18.534
&gt;&gt; I mean, this is the

00:05:18.668 --> 00:05:20.736
interesting question here.

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:22.104
I mean, you have two of some of

00:05:22.238 --> 00:05:23.706
the more prominent members of

00:05:23.839 --> 00:05:28.844
the Republican

00:05:28.978 --> 00:05:31.948
similarly spoken views,

00:05:32.081 --> 00:05:32.882
separating themselves from

00:05:33.015 --> 00:05:33.783
potentially the rest of the

00:05:33.916 --> 00:05:34.283
pack.

00:05:34.417 --> 00:05:36.686
But I wonder too, just that

00:05:36.819 --> 00:05:38.187
wording of territorial dispute.

00:05:38.321 --> 00:05:39.956
This reflects the concern of

00:05:40.089 --> 00:05:41.891
many Republicans on the hill, as

00:05:42.024 --> 00:05:43.159
well as many foreign policy

00:05:43.292 --> 00:05:43.726
experts.

00:05:43.759 --> 00:05:46.562
Say you do at one point have

00:05:46.696 --> 00:05:47.930
higher office, even if you get

00:05:48.064 --> 00:05:49.732
to a point of needing to

00:05:49.865 --> 00:05:51.367
advocate for it, even if you

00:05:51.734 --> 00:05:52.335
don't agree with this.

00:05:52.468 --> 00:05:55.071
To say territorial dispute now

00:05:55.204 --> 00:05:56.639
really belittles this war at

00:05:56.772 --> 00:05:57.273
this point.

00:05:57.406 --> 00:05:59.075
If you're in a position in the

00:05:59.208 --> 00:06:00.609
future where you are trying to

00:06:00.743 --> 00:06:03.245
advocate for foreign aid, and

00:06:03.379 --> 00:06:05.214
U.S. Support of this war, and

00:06:05.348 --> 00:06:07.216
somebody who is opposed to it

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:11.287
might bring up the fact that

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:14.890
hey, you once called this a

00:06:15.024 --> 00:06:17.360
territorial dispute.

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:19.195
&gt;&gt; Trump was able to drive his

00:06:19.328 --> 00:06:21.764
party away from free trade in

00:06:21.764 --> 00:06:22.298
2016.

00:06:22.431 --> 00:06:24.100
He's very persuadable with his

00:06:24.233 --> 00:06:24.967
base of support.

00:06:25.101 --> 00:06:27.770
And he's been waging this sort

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:30.439
of like quest to isolate the

00:06:30.573 --> 00:06:32.475
country from foreign

00:06:32.608 --> 00:06:32.908
entanglements.

00:06:33.042 --> 00:06:34.944
I think it's a very dangerous

00:06:35.077 --> 00:06:35.778
policy for Republicans.

00:06:35.778 --> 00:06:38.414
&gt;&gt; It's definitely risky for

00:06:38.547 --> 00:06:39.982
Desantis to take this position.

00:06:40.116 --> 00:06:41.817
If I look at the types of

00:06:41.951 --> 00:06:44.053
Republican voters who lean more

00:06:44.186 --> 00:06:45.421
towards Desantis than Donald

00:06:45.788 --> 00:06:46.956
Trump, they're split on this

00:06:47.089 --> 00:06:47.423
issue.

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:48.357
I've been asking this question

00:06:48.491 --> 00:06:50.126
for over a year, do you think

00:06:50.259 --> 00:06:52.795
this is in the U.S.' vital

00:06:52.928 --> 00:06:54.263
national interest to support

00:06:54.397 --> 00:06:55.164
Ukraine?

00:06:55.297 --> 00:06:57.333
They're pretty split with

00:06:57.466 --> 00:06:58.000
Desantis voters.

00:06:58.134 --> 00:07:00.469
Does he push them into saying

00:07:00.603 --> 00:07:02.438
Nikki Haley or Mike pence's

00:07:02.571 --> 00:07:02.738
arms?

00:07:02.872 --> 00:07:04.040
On the other hand, the trend

00:07:04.173 --> 00:07:06.509
line has moved.

00:07:06.642 --> 00:07:08.711
It used to be only a third of

00:07:08.844 --> 00:07:09.445
Republicans said I don't think

00:07:09.812 --> 00:07:10.579
that's in our interest.

00:07:10.713 --> 00:07:12.348
That's risen to almost half.

00:07:12.481 --> 00:07:14.583
So if Ron Desantis is headed

00:07:14.717 --> 00:07:15.818
where he thinks that trend line

00:07:15.818 --> 00:07:16.752
will continue going, where he

00:07:16.886 --> 00:07:19.955
thinks a year from now we may be

00:07:20.089 --> 00:07:22.024
asking this question again, he

00:07:22.158 --> 00:07:22.958
may be trying to "Skate where

00:07:23.092 --> 00:07:23.893
the puck is going."

00:07:24.026 --> 00:07:25.828
&gt;&gt; I think this is becoming the

00:07:25.861 --> 00:07:27.496
fault line in the Republican

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:28.197
party.

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:30.599
It's easy for somebody like

00:07:30.733 --> 00:07:32.268
speaker Mccarthy to say no blank

00:07:32.401 --> 00:07:32.868
check for Ukraine.

00:07:33.002 --> 00:07:36.005
What does that mean?

00:07:36.138 --> 00:07:37.840
As the primaries play out, the

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:39.175
candidates are going to have to

00:07:39.308 --> 00:07:40.242
get more specific about what

00:07:40.376 --> 00:07:40.943
they think and believe.

00:07:41.077 --> 00:07:44.180
What is the territorial dispute?

00:07:44.313 --> 00:07:46.916
What is our responsibility when

00:07:47.049 --> 00:07:47.850
it comes to Ukraine?

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:49.318
Is democracy at stake in the

00:07:49.452 --> 00:07:50.019
world or not?

00:07:50.152 --> 00:07:51.854
I mean, I think these are

00:07:51.954 --> 00:07:52.855
questions that have to be asked.

00:07:52.988 --> 00:07:54.690
&gt;&gt; There's also going to be a

00:07:54.824 --> 00:07:56.759
burden on the white house to

00:07:56.892 --> 00:07:59.161
keep making the case for

00:07:59.295 --> 00:08:01.330
democracy, and why we're there,

00:08:01.464 --> 00:08:03.933
and why this, a, should not be

00:08:04.066 --> 00:08:06.202
in dispute.

00:08:06.335 --> 00:08:09.405
And Kevin Mccarthy, I'm sure,

00:08:09.538 --> 00:08:11.207
was happy.

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:13.209
&gt;&gt; So two of the first

00:08:13.342 --> 00:08:16.078
Republican congressman to

00:08:16.212 --> 00:08:19.248
endorse Donald Trump, have now

00:08:19.381 --> 00:08:20.216
endorsed Ron Desantis.

00:08:20.349 --> 00:08:23.919
And today, congressman chip Roy

00:08:24.053 --> 00:08:27.890
formally endorsed Desantis.

00:08:27.890 --> 00:08:29.892
Again, Desantis has not

00:08:29.892 --> 00:08:30.826
announced he's running.

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:33.095
But congressman Roy wrote the

00:08:33.229 --> 00:08:34.530
next president must be a vie

00:08:34.663 --> 00:08:37.366
brant and energetic leader with

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:38.634
the vision to chart a new

00:08:38.767 --> 00:08:38.968
course.

00:08:39.101 --> 00:08:40.069
That leader is Ron Desantis.

00:08:40.202 --> 00:08:42.204
I have to believe that is wish

00:08:42.338 --> 00:08:42.538
casting.

00:08:42.671 --> 00:08:44.106
He wants Desantis to run.

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:46.909
&gt;&gt; Desantis hasn't announced

00:08:47.042 --> 00:08:47.376
yet.

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:50.546
It also didn't stop a former

00:08:50.679 --> 00:08:52.047
trump deputy secretary of

00:08:52.181 --> 00:08:55.251
homeland security supporting Ron

00:08:55.384 --> 00:08:57.586
Desantis in Ken cucinelli.

00:08:57.920 --> 00:08:59.255
&gt;&gt; I didn't even know that.

00:08:59.388 --> 00:09:01.290
&gt;&gt; Look, right now, you see that

00:09:01.423 --> 00:09:03.926
there are many members of the

00:09:04.059 --> 00:09:05.427
Republican party that still

00:09:05.561 --> 00:09:07.163
don't want to lose.

00:09:07.296 --> 00:09:09.031
So many people that supported

